    "raw_text": "\n<think>\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt.\n\nThe text prompt describes a 15-second, 9:16 vertical video of a female dancer in a burgundy long dress performing near a white spiral sculpture in an art gallery, with natural light from skylights, and a single dancer throughout. The evaluation below reflects the video as a whole rather than frame-by-frame details.\n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\n- The overall visual quality is moderate (3/5). The frames are generally clear with decent lighting and natural color rendition, but there are occasional minor artifacts or slight softness that prevent a higher rating.\n- Lighting remains consistent across the sequence, with believable shadows from the skylights; no major distortions or color shifts are evident.\n- The dancer's pose and movement appear plausible, and the environment reads as a clean, well-lit gallery space. Overall, the visuals are acceptable but not exceptional.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\n- The video aligns very closely with the prompt: a single female dancer in a burgundy long dress near a white spiral sculpture in a gallery setting, with natural light and a continuous performance. The alignment is strong and effectively matches all key elements, supporting a top score for this dimension.\n\nPhysical/Common-sense Consistency Analysis:\n- The scene maintains coherent physical behavior: the dancer's movements flow naturally, the dress moves plausibly, and spatial relationships to the sculpture and floor remain consistent. Lighting and shadows behave realistically, and there are no obvious physics violations. However, given the static-frame assessment, some dynamic interactions could exist beyond these frames, so the overall consistency is solid but not perfect (4/5).\n\nGround-truth scores:\n- Visual Quality: 3\n- Text-to-Video Alignment: 5\n- Physical Consistency: 4\n\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality — clarity, stability, and visible artifacts across the whole clip.3\n(2) text-to-video alignment — whether the clip shows the subject, action, and scene in the prompt.5\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency — whether visible motion and object relations follow everyday physics and common sense.4\n",
